= Concentrated liquidity =

== Overview ==
'''Concentrated liquidity''' is a market-making design in which liquidity providers allocate capital to selected price intervals rather than supplying the same liquidity across the entire possible price range.

Liquidity inside the active price range can create greater depth per unit of capital than uniformly distributed liquidity. When market price leaves a position's range, that position stops contributing active liquidity under the range-based design.

Concentration increases provider choice but also makes positions more path- and range-dependent. Providers may need to select ranges, rebalance, and manage the risk of ending with more of one asset as prices move.

Uniswap v3 introduced a widely used implementation of this idea for decentralized exchanges, but the general concept should not be defined as the Uniswap product itself.

== Boundaries ==
* concentrated liquidity ≠ Uniswap by identity
* capital efficiency ≠ guaranteed LP profitability
* out-of-range position ≠ vanished assets

